                {"question": "What is the purpose of a notes column next to your growth assumptions?", "options": ["It is purely decorative", "It documents the reasoning so anyone reviewing the model can evaluate whether the assumption is defensible", "Excel requires notes to calculate formulas", "It replaces the need for an Assumptions tab"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Documented reasoning lets a reviewer judge whether an assumption is credible, which is central to professional modeling."},
                {"question": "In the formula =PriorYearRevenue*(1+GrowthRateAssumption), where should GrowthRateAssumption come from?", "options": ["Typed directly into the formula as a number", "A cell reference on the Assumptions tab", "It should be omitted entirely", "The company's stock price"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Referencing an assumptions cell keeps the model dynamic and consistent with proper modeling conventions."}
